    "title": "bip98: fix the third SKIP hash in the example proof",
    "user": {
      "login": "0xShadowX",
      "id": 146137079,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOCLXf9w",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146137079?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/0xShadowX",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/0xShadowX",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/0xShadowX/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/0xShadowX/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/0xShadowX/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/0xShadowX/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/0xShadowX/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/0xShadowX/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/0xShadowX/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/0xShadowX/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/0xShadowX/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The example in the Inclusion Proofs section lists the skipped hashes as 0x00..., 0x66... and 0x22..., in that order, and the diagram source (`bip-0098/traversal-example.dot`) agrees: 0x22... is the SKIP branch of D. The base64 proof under it decodes to `06 bd8440 03`, then 32 bytes of 0x00, 32 of 0x66 and 32 of 0x44. 0x44... is E's right child, which is a VERIFY hash and shouldn't be in the proof.\n\nThis re-encodes the proof with 0x22... as the third hash. The header, the node codes and the 101-byte length stay the same, only the last 32 bytes change. It also drops a stray \".\" after \"base64:\".\n\n```\npython3 -c \"import base64; print(base64.b64encode(bytes.fromhex('06bd844003')+b'\\x00'*32+b'\\x66'*32+b'\\x22'*32).decode())\"\n```\n",
